    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-30T18:30:32.497Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "Market sizing and adoption signals for agentic commerce (per LI.FI):\n\n- **McKinsey: $3\u20135 trillion opportunity by 2030** for global agentic commerce, including **$900 billion to $1 trillion in orchestrated B2B revenue in the US**\n- Enterprise/B2B use cases progressing faster than retail; consumer implementation expected unevenly **2026\u20132028**\n- Cautionary consumer signal: OpenAI's first-generation Instant Checkout attracted only ~30 Shopify merchants before pivoting in March 2026\n- Industrial precedent: Denso has made autonomous purchases via Skyfire since August 2024\n- VC framing: a16z \u2014 the shift from \"something you ask\" to \"something that does\"; Sequoia \u2014 services ($6 spent per $1 of software) favor outcome-delivery agents\n\nSource: LI.FI, \"The Agentic Economy \u2014 A Deep Dive\" (https://li.fi/knowledge-hub/the-agentic-economy-%E2%80%94-a-deep-dive).",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-30T12:10:00.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-30T18:30:32.497Z"
    }
  },
