  {
    "index": 12,
    "hash": "JK+XTIixAxlnt9EsaZ6bqZSNd4o=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T10:14:55.628Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "Market sizing and adoption signals for agentic commerce (per LI.FI):\n\n- **McKinsey: $3\u20135 trillion opportunity by 2030** for global agentic commerce, including **$900 billion to $1 trillion in orchestrated B2B revenue in the US**\n- Enterprise/B2B use cases progressing faster than retail; consumer implementation expected unevenly **2026\u20132028**\n- Cautionary consumer signal: OpenAI's first-generation Instant Checkout attracted only ~30 Shopify merchants before pivoting in March 2026\n- Industrial precedent: Denso has made autonomous purchases via Skyfire since August 2024\n- VC framing: a16z \u2014 the shift from \"something you ask\" to \"something that does\"; Sequoia \u2014 services ($6 spent per $1 of software) favor outcome-delivery agents\n\nSource: LI.FI, \"The Agentic Economy \u2014 A Deep Dive\" (https://li.fi/knowledge-hub/the-agentic-economy-%E2%80%94-a-deep-dive).\n\n## Boundary: the bull and bear cases measure different things\nThese two forecasts are routinely read as contradictory and are not. McKinsey sizes a **market** in 2030; Gartner counts **project mortality** by end-2027. A shakeout that kills more than 40% of initiatives while the surviving use cases compound into trillions is the ordinary shape of an infrastructure build-out, not a paradox \u2014 and both sources agree on the mechanism, that the rails are ahead of demand and value concentrates where outcomes are objectively verifiable.\n\nWhat the pair does establish is that **neither number is settled**: the vault should carry them as a scenario range, not as a projection. The discriminating evidence is B2B adoption data in 2027-2028, which is when the two forecasts stop being compatible \u2014 if enterprise orchestration has not compounded by then, the bear case was the base case.\n",
        "updatedAt": "2026-09-03T10:14:55.628Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T10:14:55.628Z"
    }
  }
